  data: {
    LLM: "After the deal, players may call for a partner (holder of black queens), go alone (zola, stealer, or zola schneider/schwartz), or announce Schneider. Player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit; if unable, must play trump. Highest trump wins, else highest card of led suit. Winner of trick leads next. Eight tricks per hand; trick points (A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2, 9/8/7=0) determine game points.",
    Player: "After the deal, players may call for a partner (holder of black queens), go alone (zola, stealer, or zola schneider/schwartz), or announce Schneider. Player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit; if unable, must play trump. Highest trump wins, else highest card of led suit. Winner of trick leads next. Eight tricks per hand; trick points (A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2, 9/8/7=0) determine game points.",
    objective: 'Win tricks containing valuable cards; be the first to reach 42 or more game points. Partnerships are temporary each hand (two vs two, or one vs three if a player goes alone).',
    gameplay: "After the deal, players may call for a partner (holder of black queens), go alone (zola, stealer, or zola schneider/schwartz), or announce Schneider. Player to dealer's left leads; must follow suit; if unable, must play trump. Highest trump wins, else highest card of led suit. Winner of trick leads next. Eight tricks per hand; trick points (A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2, 9/8/7=0) determine game points.",
    keyRules: [
      '14 trumps: all queens, jacks, and diamonds; rank high to low: Club Q, Diamond 7 (Spitzer), Spade Q, Heart Q, Diamond Q, Club J, Spade J, Heart J, Diamond J, Diamond A, 10, K, 9, 8.',
      'Non-trump (fail) in each suit rank A, 10, K, 9, 8, 7.',
